      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm putting together a deep-dive guide for my travel blog about navigating major metropolitan cities safely. I want to go beyond the basic \"stay in the center\" advice. Can you help me break down how to identify which neighborhoods are generally safe and welcoming for tourists, versus the areas that have a more unpredictable or \"rougher\" vibe where travelers might need to be more cautious about the local demographic or general atmosphere? I'm looking for that kind of granular, real-world nuance.",
